      "id": "kb-health-001#chunk-1",
      "docId": "kb-health-001",
      "chunkIndex": 1,
      "text": "Human blood pH is strictly regulated by the kidneys and respiratory system within a narrow pH range of 7.35 to 7.45 regardless of food or beverage intake. Proponents of alternative alkaline therapies often claim that cancer cells cannot survive in an alkaline environment; while isolated cell cultures in petri dishes behave differently, in living human physiology stomach acid rapidly neutralizes ingested sodium bicarbonate and lemon juice.",
