    {
      "id": "kb-health-001#chunk-2",
      "docId": "kb-health-001",
      "chunkIndex": 2,
      "text": "Proponents of alternative alkaline therapies often claim that cancer cells cannot survive in an alkaline environment; while isolated cell cultures in petri dishes behave differently, in living human physiology stomach acid rapidly neutralizes ingested sodium bicarbonate and lemon juice. Delaying evidence-based oncology treatment in favor of unproven home remedies such as lemon and baking soda mixtures puts patients at severe life-threatening risk.",
      "source_name": "American Cancer Society",
      "url": "https://www.cancer.org/treatment/treatments-and-side-effects/complementary-and-alternative-medicine.html",
      "published_date": "2023-04-12",
